```java
// (1) Double-checked locking with volatile
class ConfigManager {
    private static volatile ConfigManager instance; // volatile: safe publication
    private final Map<String, String> settings;
    private ConfigManager() { settings = Map.of("maxItems", "50"); }

    static ConfigManager getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {                       // first check (no lock)
            synchronized (ConfigManager.class) {
                if (instance == null) {               // second check (locked)
                    instance = new ConfigManager();
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }
    String get(String key) { return settings.get(key); }
}

// (2) Enum Singleton — simplest and safest (Effective Java)
enum Config {
    INSTANCE;                                          // one constant for this loaded enum class
    private final Map<String, String> settings = Map.of("maxItems", "50");
    String get(String key) { return settings.get(key); }
}
```

*`volatile` prevents another thread seeing a half-constructed object; the enum relies on Java class-initialization and enum-serialization rules.*

