// Loaded once, immutable afterwards -> a legitimate Singleton resource.
enum DiscountRuleEngine {
    INSTANCE;
    private final Map<String, Double> rules = loadRulesOnce(); // expensive, done once
    double rateFor(String code) { return rules.getOrDefault(code, 0.0); }
    private static Map<String, Double> loadRulesOnce() { return Map.of("STUDENT", 0.15); }
}

// Per-user data is passed explicitly, not stored in a Singleton:
double price(String userId, String code, double base) {
    return base * (1 - DiscountRuleEngine.INSTANCE.rateFor(code)); // shared, read-only
}
```

*Share the expensive, unique resource; pass per-request data as parameters.*

