```java
class Config {
    private static final Config INSTANCE = new Config();
    private Config() {}
    static Config getInstance() { return INSTANCE; }
}

// An attacker (or careless code) can create a SECOND instance:
Constructor<Config> c = Config.class.getDeclaredConstructor();
c.setAccessible(true);          // bypasses private
Config second = c.newInstance(); // breaks the singleton guarantee
```

```java
public enum CartConfig {
    INSTANCE;                                  // one constant for this loaded enum class

    private final Map<String, String> settings;
    private final int maxItems;
    CartConfig() {                              // private by definition
        settings = Map.of("maxItems", "50", "currency", "USD");
        maxItems = Integer.parseInt(settings.get("maxItems"));
    }
    public String get(String key) { return settings.get(key); }
    public boolean isFull(int count) { return count >= maxItems; }
}

// Usage — clean, and reflection cannot create a second instance:
boolean full = CartConfig.INSTANCE.isFull(45);
// Constructor.newInstance() on an enum throws IllegalArgumentException.
```

*No `volatile`, locking, or `readResolve` is needed for the declared enum constant; the boundary is the loaded enum class.*
